WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.391
Step 1. Open the encounter. In All Encounters, select View Encounter.

1.2
00:00:05.391 --> 00:00:10.308
The list shows only encounters created today, so for an older one,

1.3
00:00:10.308 --> 00:00:18.251
search the patient's identifier and use Look up a patient.

2.1
00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:23.548
Step 2. Open the Service Requests tab. Select the Service Requests tab.

2.2
00:00:23.548 --> 00:00:28.171
Care creates the new service request under this encounter.

3.1
00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:33.141
Step 3. Start a new service request. Select Create Service Request.

3.2
00:00:33.141 --> 00:00:37.509
Care shows this button only while the encounter is still open,

3.3
00:00:37.509 --> 00:00:40.475
and opens the Service Request form.

4.1
00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:43.598
Step 4. Select the activity definition.

4.2
00:00:43.598 --> 00:00:47.061
Select Select Activity Definition and pick one.

4.3
00:00:47.061 --> 00:00:51.039
Care adds a card and copies the title, category, code,

4.4
00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:55.444
body site and locations from the activity definition.

5.1
00:00:55.444 --> 00:00:57.716
Step 5. Complete the card.

5.2
00:00:57.716 --> 00:01:02.303
Care adds the card closed, so select it to open its fields.

5.3
00:01:02.303 --> 00:01:07.312
Priority is Routine by default, and you are the requester.

6.1
00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:11.445
Step 7. Save the service requests. Select Save Changes.

6.2
00:01:11.445 --> 00:01:17.235
Care opens the Overview of the encounter and creates a charge item for each charge

6.3
00:01:17.235 --> 00:01:21.265
item definition linked to the activity definition.
